{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The voice of your brother's bloods.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: his blood and the blood of his descendants (דמו ודם זרעיותיו). And this Midrash alludes to the resurrection of the dead, for once he died, his offspring were no longer within his power — so where is the blood of his descendants? Rather, the matter alludes to the resurrection of the dead at the end. Or the blood of his descendants alludes to the matter known in the Kabbalah, concerning which Scripture said of Sheth, 'in place of Abel' (בשת תחת הבל). And behold, the punishment of Cain was measure for measure: he plotted to cut off his brother's seed, and he and his seed were cut off in the Flood."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:14.809177942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}